{% only_dark %}
![Appwrite Beep on a tablet and a phone, showing firing alerts, alert activity, and project usage for Acme Inc](/images/docs/beep/dark/overview.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Appwrite Beep on a tablet and a phone, showing firing alerts, alert activity, and project usage for Acme Inc](/images/docs/beep/overview.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Appwrite Beep is the Appwrite Cloud app for your phone. It sends a push when one of your [monitors](/docs/products/monitors) fires, shows what is firing across your organizations, and keeps project usage and the Appwrite changelog one tap away.

Beep is built for reading and triage. Acknowledging an alert, snoozing pushes, and adjusting a threshold happen in the app, and anything else opens the Appwrite Console.

- [Download on the App Store](https://apps.apple.com/app/id6831213827) for iPhone and iPad
- [Get it on Google Play](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=io.appwrite.beep) for Android phones, tablets, and foldables

# Set up Beep {% #set-up %}

{% only_dark %}
![The Choose what you watch and What reaches you setup screens in Beep](/images/docs/beep/dark/setup.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The Choose what you watch and What reaches you setup screens in Beep](/images/docs/beep/setup.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Sign in with your Appwrite Cloud account, using GitHub, Google, or email and password. Accounts with multi-factor authentication get the same MFA challenge as the Console.

On first launch, Beep walks through a short setup. Any step can be skipped, and Home keeps a checklist of what's left.

1. **Choose what you watch.** Pick the organizations and projects Beep notifies you about. New organizations and projects are watched automatically.
2. **Choose what reaches you.** Firing alerts always reach you. Resolved alerts and product updates are optional.
3. **Turn on notifications** and, on Android, critical alerts.
4. **Send a test alert** to confirm pushes reach the phone.

These settings belong to your Appwrite account, so they apply on every device you sign in on.

# Push notifications {% #push-notifications %}

{% only_dark %}
![A critical push for an egress spike on storefront-prod with Acknowledge and Open alert buttons](/images/docs/beep/dark/push.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![A critical push for an egress spike on storefront-prod with Acknowledge and Open alert buttons](/images/docs/beep/push.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Beep registers each phone you sign in on as a push target on your Appwrite account. When a monitor fires, every registered phone gets a push that names the severity, the monitor, and where it fired.

The buttons on a push work without opening the app:

| Push | Buttons |
| --- | --- |
| Firing alert | **Acknowledge**, **Snooze 1 hour**, **Mute** |
| Critical alert | **Acknowledge**, **Open alert** |
| Resolved alert | **Mute** |

Each button is undoable from the notification it leaves behind. A critical push leaves out snoozing and muting, so a half-awake tap can't quiet an incident. Both stay available inside the alert.

# Alerts {% #alerts %}

{% only_dark %}
![The Alerts tab listing firing alerts for Acme Inc, with the Egress spike alert enlarged](/images/docs/beep/dark/alerts.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The Alerts tab listing firing alerts for Acme Inc, with the Egress spike alert enlarged](/images/docs/beep/alerts.avif)
{% /only_light %}

The **Alerts** tab lists firing, acknowledged, and resolved alerts for each organization. It covers usage and budget monitors and HTTP, DNS, TCP, and SMTP checks. Search and filters narrow the list, and **History** shows alerts that already resolved.

Open an alert to see the reading that fired it, a chart of the hours around it, and where its escalation stands. **Acknowledge** tells your team someone is on it and stops the escalation. Long press an alert in the list for quick actions.

# Escalations {% #escalations %}

{% only_dark %}
![The On-call escalation in Beep, with its two steps enlarged](/images/docs/beep/dark/escalation.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The On-call escalation in Beep, with its two steps enlarged](/images/docs/beep/escalation.avif)
{% /only_light %}

An escalation notifies its steps in turn while nobody has acknowledged an alert. Each step names who to notify and how long to wait after the step before it.

Open **Policy** on an alert to see the escalations in its organization. From there, create an escalation, edit its steps and repeats, or assign it to a monitor.

# Thresholds {% #thresholds %}

{% only_dark %}
![The Egress spike alert next to the Adjust threshold sheet raising the threshold from 5 GB to 6 GB](/images/docs/beep/dark/threshold.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The Egress spike alert next to the Adjust threshold sheet raising the threshold from 5 GB to 6 GB](/images/docs/beep/threshold.avif)
{% /only_light %}

A usage alert shows the threshold it crossed. Tap **Adjust** to raise or lower it from the alert. The sheet charts recent usage against the new value before you save.

# Critical alerts {% #critical-alerts %}

{% only_dark %}
![The Ring for what matters setup screen and the Critical alerts settings screen in Beep](/images/docs/beep/dark/critical.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The Ring for what matters setup screen and the Critical alerts settings screen in Beep](/images/docs/beep/critical.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Monitors set to **Critical** ring on silent, at alarm volume. Everything else arrives as a normal notification.

1. In the Appwrite Console, set a usage monitor's severity or a budget threshold to **Critical**.
2. On Android, tap **Override Do Not Disturb** during setup, or open **Settings** > **Critical alerts** in Beep. Android asks you to allow it for the **Critical alerts** channel.
3. Set your alarm volume. Critical alerts ring at that volume.

# Snooze notifications {% #snooze %}

{% only_dark %}
![Beep Home suggesting to snooze notifications after 7 notifications in 30 minutes](/images/docs/beep/dark/snooze.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Beep Home suggesting to snooze notifications after 7 notifications in 30 minutes](/images/docs/beep/snooze.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Snoozing pauses pushes from one organization, or all of them, while you handle an incident. Alerts keep firing and still show in Beep, the Console, and email. Snooze for **30 minutes**, **1 hour**, **4 hours**, or **24 hours**.

- **From Home.** When pushes pile up, Home offers to snooze them.
- **From a push.** Tap **Snooze 1 hour**.
- **From Settings.** Open **Settings** > **Snooze** to pick the organization and length.
- **From the app icon.** Long press it and choose **Snooze for 1 hour**.

Beep tells you when the snooze ends, with a button to snooze again.

# Projects {% #projects %}

{% only_dark %}
![The storefront-prod project in Beep, with its requests chart over 24 hours enlarged](/images/docs/beep/dark/project.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The storefront-prod project in Beep, with its requests chart over 24 hours enlarged](/images/docs/beep/project.avif)
{% /only_light %}

The **Projects** tab lists each project with its requests over the last 24 hours, and projects with firing alerts come first. Open a project to chart bandwidth, requests, storage, executions, and compute over **24h**, **7d**, or **30d**, each against the period before it.

# Monitors {% #monitors %}

{% only_dark %}
![The Checkout API health check in Beep, failing with an unexpected status code](/images/docs/beep/dark/monitor.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The Checkout API health check in Beep, failing with an unexpected status code](/images/docs/beep/monitor.avif)
{% /only_light %}

The **Monitors** tab lists every monitor in an organization with its latest reading: usage monitors, budget thresholds, and endpoint checks. Open a check to see what it targets, when it fires, how often it runs, and, for HTTPS, when its certificate expires.

Monitors are created in the Appwrite Console. Learn more in [Monitors](/docs/products/monitors).

# Updates {% #updates %}

{% only_dark %}
![The Updates tab in Beep with Cloud status and the latest changelog entry enlarged](/images/docs/beep/dark/updates.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![The Updates tab in Beep with Cloud status and the latest changelog entry enlarged](/images/docs/beep/updates.avif)
{% /only_light %}

The **Updates** tab shows ongoing Appwrite Cloud incidents and the [Appwrite changelog](/changelog). With **Product updates** on, Beep sends a push when a new changelog entry goes live, and tapping it opens the entry.

# Tablets and foldables {% #tablets %}

{% only_dark %}
![Beep's dashboard layout on a tablet, with alerts, activity, projects, and firing alerts side by side](/images/docs/beep/dark/tablet.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Beep's dashboard layout on a tablet, with alerts, activity, projects, and firing alerts side by side](/images/docs/beep/tablet.avif)
{% /only_light %}

On iPad, Android tablets, and open foldables, Beep switches to a dashboard layout that follows the window width. Home puts activity, projects, firing alerts, and the latest changelog entry side by side.

# Settings {% #settings %}

{% only_dark %}
![Beep Settings with the Snooze, Product updates, and Resolved alerts options enlarged](/images/docs/beep/dark/settings.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Beep Settings with the Snooze, Product updates, and Resolved alerts options enlarged](/images/docs/beep/settings.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Open **Settings** from the gear on any tab.

- **This phone.** Notification permission, critical alerts, and **Check setup**, which sends a test alert.
- **Notifications.** Snooze, product updates, and resolved alerts.
- **Organizations.** Turn pushes on or off for each organization.
- **Share usage analytics.** Beep sends anonymous usage analytics without IDs or names. Turn it off here.

Notification settings belong to your Appwrite account. The same options appear in the Console: click the bell in the header, then the gear, and find **Mobile pushes**.
